@node Requirements
@chapter Requirements

@cindex Requirements

Casual Symbol Overlay requires @uref{https://github.com/magit/transient, Transient} 0.9+. Versions of GNU Emacs 30.1 or greater will satisfy this requirement with its built-in version of Transient.

The following packages are also required but will be installed as dependencies if not present.

@itemize
@item
@uref{https://github.com/kickingvegas/casual, Casual} ≥ 3.0.0
@item
@uref{https://github.com/wolray/symbol-overlay, Symbol Overlay} ≥ 4.2    
@end itemize

Casual Symbol Overlay has been verified with the following configuration.

@itemize
@item
GNU Emacs 31.1 (macOS 15.7@comma{} Ubuntu Linux 22.04.5 LTS)
@item
Symbol Overlay 4.3
@end itemize

@node Install
@chapter Install

@cindex Install

Casual Symbol Overlay is intended to be installed via @code{package-install} from MELPA@comma{} either directly or as a dependency to @uref{https://github.com/kickingvegas/casual-suite, Casual Suite}. After this installation@comma{} Casual Symbol Overlay can be setup in a number of ways@comma{} as enumerated in the sub-sections below.

@menu
* Setup with Casual Suite::
* Setup with Casual only::
* Setup Casual Symbol Overlay only::
* Manual Install::
@end menu

@node Setup with Casual Suite
@section Setup with Casual Suite

If you have Casual Symbol Overlay installed as a dependency to @uref{https://github.com/kickingvegas/casual-suite, Casual Suite}@comma{} then Casual Suite will automatically setup Casual Symbol Overlay. Refer to the Casual Suite @uref{https://github.com/kickingvegas/casual-suite#install, Install section} for more detail.

Note that this will only work if Casual Symbol Overlay is installed via @code{package-install}.

@node Setup with Casual only
@section Setup with Casual only

Casual Symbol Overlay includes the base Casual package as a dependency. Casual has the command @code{casual-init} which will setup all modules within it as specified in the hook variable @code{casual-init-hook}. Casual Symbol Overlay can be included in this hook with the following Elisp added to your Emacs initialization file:

@lisp
(add-hook 'casual-init-hook #'casual-symbol-overlay-init)
@end lisp

Note that this will only work if Casual Symbol Overlay is installed via @code{package-install}.

@node Setup Casual Symbol Overlay only
@section Setup Casual Symbol Overlay only

If only setup for Casual Symbol Overlay is desired@comma{} then directly run the command @code{casual-avy-init}@comma{} either manually with @code{extended-execute-command} (@code{M-x}) or by adding it to your Emacs initialization file.

@lisp
(casual-symbol-overlay-init)
@end lisp

Note that this will only work if Casual Symbol Overlay is installed via @code{package-install}.

@node Manual Install
@section Manual Install

Casual Symbol Overlay is installed outside of @code{package-install}@comma{} then add the following lines to your Emacs initialization file.

@lisp
(require 'casual-symbol-overlay) ;; optional if using autoloaded menu
(keymap-set symbol-overlay-map casual-keybinding-primary #'casual-symbol-overlay-tmenu)
@end lisp

